s/photos/1076655-.1.jpg','youtube',NULL,'','<p>Wittmann Ries 0.75L, Limestone Rocks, Riesling, Rheinhessen, QbA, dry, white (Screwcap, Organic)</p><p></p><p>This wine from the Wittmann winery is part of a range of excellent wines created exclusively for Gebr. Heinemann. \"Limestone rocks\" is an ingenious play on words between \"limestone\", the soil on which this wine grows and \"rock\" which is called \"rock\" or \"rocks\". In English, \"rocks\" can also stand for \"get carried away\" or \"be super\". Because the Wittmann family are convinced that limestone soils are the best subsoil for their Rieslings.</p><p></p><p>Fine aroma of pale fruits and apple, an elegant clear structure with a juicy freshness. Dry with a luscious acidity which harmonises well with the typically earthy mineral tones, followed by a good finish. An essential Riesling for everyday drinking. Serving temperature: 6–8°C. Works supremely well with vegetables and fish, or on its own simply for fun.</p><p></p><p>Made in Germany</p>',37.00,0.00,0,'[]','[]','[]',NULL,0,1,0,0,'1076655',1,7.00,'amount',NULL,'amount','0',0.00,0.00,14,'Wittmann Ries 0.75L, Limestone Rocks, Riesling, Rheinhessen, QbA, dry, white (screwcap, organic)','<p>Wittmann Ries 0.75L, Limestone Rocks, Riesling, Rheinhessen, QbA, dry, white (Screwcap, Organic)</p><p></p><p>This wine from the Wittmann winery is part of a range of excellent wines created exclusively for Gebr. Heinemann. \"Limestone rocks\" is an ingenious play on words between \"limestone\", the soil on which this wine grows and \"rock\" which is called \"rock\" or \"rocks\". In English, \"rocks\" can also stand for \"get carried away\" or \"be super\". Because the Wittmann family are convinced that limestone soils are the best subsoil for their Rieslings.</p><p></p><p>Fine aroma of pale fruits and apple, an elegant clear structure with a juicy freshness. Dry with a luscious acidity which harmonises well with the typically earthy mineral tones, followed by a good finish. An essential Riesling for everyday drinking. Serving temperature: 6–8°C. Works supremely well with vegetables and fish, or on its own simply for fun.</p><p></p><p>Made in Germany</p>','uploads/products/photos/1076655-.1.jpg',NULL,'wittmann-ries-0-75l-limestone-rocks-riesling-rheinhessen-qba-dry-white-screwcap-organic--1076655',0,0.00,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,'2020-12-04 07:22:42','2020-12-15 13:52:32',0),(1075,'St Hugo Shiraz 0.75L,','seller',203,12,79,NULL,194,'[\"uploads\\/products\\/photos\\/1274264-.1.jpg\"]','uploads/products/photos/1274264-.1.jpg','youtube',NULL,'','<p>St Hugo Shiraz, red, 0.75L</p><p></p><p>St Hugo wines are crafted from the finest parcels of fruit from Coonawarra and the Barossa Valley. These fine Australian red wines are lauded for their depth, intensity and ability to age gracefully. Matured separately in 53% new French oak and 21% new American oak and the balance in used oak for 19 months, this wine is beautifully balanced, with excellent structure and length typifying the St Hugo Heritage of power and elegance.</p><p></p><p>Aroma: Classic Barossa Shiraz, with a heady and a complex mix of blackberry, plum and spice aromas which unfold over time in the glass. Palate - Bold, dark, ripe fruit with a savoury edge. Elegant fine tannins are felt across the palate and the subtle oak influence yields vanilla, cedar and charry notes on the finish.</p><p></p><p>Made in Australia</p>',82.00,0.00,0,'[]','[]','[]',NULL,0,1,0,0,'1274264',1,33.00,'amount',NULL,'amount','0',0.00,0.00,11,'St Hugo Shiraz 0.75L,','<p>St Hugo Shiraz, red, 0.75L</p><p></p><p>St Hugo wines are crafted from the finest parcels of fruit from Coonawarra and the Barossa Valley. These fine Australian red wines are lauded for their depth, intensity and ability to age gracefully. Matured separately in 53% new French oak and 21% new American oak and the balance in used oak for 19 months, this wine is beautifully balanced, with excellent structure and length typifying the St Hugo Heritage of power and elegance.</p><p></p><p>Aroma: Classic Barossa Shiraz, with a heady and a complex mix of blackberry, plum and spice aromas which unfold over time in the glass. Palate - Bold, dark, ripe fruit with a savoury edge. Elegant fine tannins are felt across the palate and the subtle oak influence yields vanilla, cedar and charry notes on the finish.</p><p></p><p>Made in Australia</p>','uploads/products/photos/1274264-.1.jpg',NULL,'st-hugo-shiraz-0-75l--1274264',0,0.00,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,'2020-12-04 07:22:43','2020-12-18 08:45:54',0),(1076,'Masi, Masianco, Pinot Grigio / Verduzzo, Veneto, IGP, dry, white, 0.75L','seller',203,12,79,NULL,193,'[\"uploads\\/products\\/photos\\/787343-.1.jpg\"]','uploads/products/photos/787343-.1.jpg','youtube',NULL,'','<p>Masi, Masianco, Pinot Grigio / Verduzzo, Veneto, IGP, dry, white, 0.75L</p><p></p><p>A new interpretation of white wines: Pinot Grigio with Appaxximento, unique white wine blend made with fresh and semi-dried grapes. Finely judged blend of the two native grape varieties; technique employed in vinification. Overripened Verduzzo (unusual technique for an elegant white wine) on racks ferments in barriques and balances the fresh acidity of Pinot Grigio. Selected grapes cultivated at Strà del Milione (Udine). Flexible wine-food pairing.</p><p></p><p>Strong pale straw-yellow colour with golden reflections. Elegant ripe fruit aromas on the nose, apricots and peaches particularly, blending into pineapple tropical fruit aromas. Good body and freshness on the palate with generous ripe fruit flavours coming through from the nose with a slight lemon twist at the end. Dry and very long on the finish.</p><p></p><p></p><p>Made in Italy</p>',28.00,0.00,0,'[]','[]','[]',NULL,0,1,0,0,'787343',1,3.00,'amount',NULL,'amount','0',0.00,0.00,9,'Masi, Masianco, Pinot Grigio / Verduzzo, Veneto, IGP, dry, white, 0.75L','<p>Masi, Masianco, Pinot Grigio / Verduzzo, Veneto, IGP, dry, white, 0.75L</p><p></p><p>A new interpretation of white wines: Pinot Grigio with Appaxximento, unique white wine blend made with fresh and semi-dried grapes. Finely judged blend of the two native grape varieties; technique employed in vinification. Overripened Verduzzo (unusual technique for an elegant white wine) on racks ferments in barriques and balances the fresh acidity of Pinot Grigio. Selected grapes cultivated at Strà del Milione (Udine). Flexible wine-food pairing.</p><p></p><p>Strong pale straw-yellow colour with golden reflections. Elegant ripe fruit aromas on the nose, apricots and peaches particularly, blending into pineapple tropical fruit aromas. Good body and freshness on the palate with generous ripe fruit flavours coming through from the nose with a slight lemon twist at the end. Dry and very long on the finish.</p><p></p><p></p><p>Made in Italy</p>','uploads/products/photos/787343-.1.jpg',NULL,'masi-masianco-pinot-grigio-verduzzo-veneto-igp-dry-white-0-75l-787343',0,0.00,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,'2020-12-04 07:22:46','2020-12-15 14:19:50',0),(1077,'Guy Saget, Sancerre, AOC, dry, white 0.75L','seller',203,12,79,NULL,192,'[\"uploads\\/products\\/photos\\/78981-.1.jpg\"]','uploads/products/photos/78981-.1.jpg','youtube',NULL,'','<p>Guy Saget, Sancerre, AOC, dry, white 0.75L</p><p></p><p>The mission of the Guy Saget brand is to demonstrate to the highest level Saget La Perrière’s intention to unravel the extreme complexity associated with the Loire vineyards. A complete collection of the finest Loire wines to satisfy the most finetuned and exacting palates, they showcase the wine range from Guy Saget, Ambassador of the Loire.</p><p></p><p>Tasting notes: Bright wine with green tints. On the nose, some aromas of white flowers predominate over a mineral frame. On the palate, the wine is generous and fresh with floral aromas.</p><p></p><p>Perfect food pairings: Grilled fish, Crottins de Chavignol goat\'s cheese,</p><p>tandoori chicken skewers, sushi & sashimi.</p><p></p><p>Serve at a temperature between 10 and 12°C</p><p></p><p>Made in France</p>',45.00,0.00,0,'[]','[]','[]',NULL,0,1,0,0,'78981',1,17.00,'amount',NULL,'amount','0',0.00,0.00,13,'Guy Saget, Sancerre, AOC, dry, white 0.75L','<p>Guy Saget, Sancerre, AOC, dry, white 0.75L</p><p></p><p>The mission of the Guy Saget brand is to demonstrate to the highest level Saget La Perrière’s intention to unravel the extreme complexity associated with the Loire vineyards. A complete collection of the finest Loire wines to satisfy the most finetuned and exacting palates, they showcase the wine range from Guy Saget, Ambassador of the Loire.</p><p></p><p>Tasting notes: Bright wine with green tints. On the nose, some aromas of white flowers predominate over a mineral frame. On the palate, the wine is generous and fresh with floral aromas.</p><p></p><p>Perfect food pairings: Grilled fish, Crottins de Chavignol goat\'s cheese,</p><p>tandoori chicken skewers, sushi & sashimi.</p><p></p><p>Serve at a temperature between 10 and 12°C</p><p></p><p>Made in France</p>','uploads/products/photos/78981-.1.jpg',NULL,'guy-saget-sancerre-aoc-dry-white-0-75l-78981',0,0.00,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,'2020-12-04 07:22:46','2020-12-17 07:22:47',0),(1112,'Yamazaki Single Malt 18 years 43% 0.7L','seller',203,12,85,NULL,191,'[\"uploads\\/products\\/photos\\/1375360-.1.jpg\"]','uploads/products/photos/1375360-.1.jpg','youtube',NULL,'','<p>Yamazaki Single Malt 18 years 43% 0.7L</p><p></p><p>Made in Japan</p>',1688.00,0.00,0,'[]','[]','[]',NULL,0,1,0,0,'1375360',1,289.00,'amount',NULL,'amount','0',0.00,0.00,0,'Yamazaki Single Malt 18 years 43% 0.7L','<p>Yamazaki Single Malt 18 years 43% 0.7L</p><p></p><p>Made in Japan</p>','uploads/products/photos/1375360-.1.jpg',NULL,'yamazaki-single-malt-18-years-43-0-7l-1375360',0,0.00,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,'2020-12-04 08:00:37','2020-12-10 17:16:08',0),(1113,'Yamazaki Single Malt 12 years 43% 0.7L','seller',203,12,85,NULL,191,'[\"uploads\\/products\\/photos\\/1375361-.1.jpg\"]','uploads/products/photos/1375361-.1.jpg','youtube',NULL,'','<p>Yamazaki