nd body make it an ideal match for meat and game dishes and for cheese.\n\nGrape variety: Nebbiolo','uploads/products/photos/IT-PB-.1.jpg',NULL,'prunotto-barolo-docg-it-pb',0,0.00,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,'2021-03-23 09:04:43','2021-04-08 05:13:18',0),(1647,'ANTINORI PEPPOLI CHIANTI CLASSICO','seller',1544,12,79,96,201,'[\"uploads\\/products\\/photos\\/IT-APCC-.1.jpg\"]','uploads/products/photos/IT-APCC-.1.jpg','youtube',NULL,'','<p>Country: Italy</p><p></p><p>This is a Chianti Classico made from Sangiovese grapes with a small addition of Merlot and Syrah, grown on the Pèppoli estate. It is designed to be drunk while the fruit is at its most expressive. It is aged in 55hl Slavonian oak barrels (10% in American oak barriques) for a maximum of 9 months, followed by a further maturing period in the bottles.</p><p></p><p>Taste: Ruby red in color with purple highlights, the wine shows intensely fruity notes of cherries and red currants on the nose which fuse very well with the typical sensations of violets which characterize Chianti Classico. Very delicate and quite well integrated the smoky sensations created by the oak aging. The palate is savory with a tasty vein of acidity together with silky and polished tannins.</p>',60.00,0.00,0,'[]','[]','[]',NULL,0,0,0,12,'IT-APCC',1,NULL,'amount',NULL,'amount','0',0.00,0.00,0,'ANTINORI PEPPOLI CHIANTI CLASSICO','Country: Italy\r\n\r\nThis is a Chianti Classico made from Sangiovese grapes with a small addition of Merlot and Syrah, grown on the Pèppoli estate. It is designed to be drunk while the fruit is at its most expressive. It is aged in 55hl Slavonian oak barrels (10% in American oak barriques) for a maximum of 9 months, followed by a further maturing period in the bottles.\r\n\r\nTaste: Ruby red in color with purple highlights, the wine shows intensely fruity notes of cherries and red currants on the nose which fuse very well with the typical sensations of violets which characterize Chianti Classico. Very delicate and quite well integrated the smoky sensations created by the oak aging. The palate is savory with a tasty vein of acidity together with silky and polished tannins.','uploads/products/photos/IT-APCC-.1.jpg',NULL,'antinori-peppoli-chianti-classico-it-apcc',0,0.00,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,'2021-03-23 09:04:43','2021-04-09 05:24:01',0),(1648,'ANTINORI BADIA A PASSIGNANO GRAN SELEZIONE CHIANTI CLASSICO RISERVA DOCG','seller',1544,12,79,96,201,'[\"uploads\\/products\\/photos\\/IT-ABPC-.1.jpg\"]','uploads/products/photos/IT-ABPC-.1.jpg','youtube',NULL,'','<p>Country: Italy</p><p></p><p>An intense ruby red in color, the wine shows aromas of ripe fruit, at times of maximum ripeness, but with a total respect for the grape variety and an excellently maintained freshness. The notes of the fruit and of the oak fuse in harmonious balance with minty balsamic notes and suggestions of graphite. The rich palate, with supple and balanced tannins, is vibrant and fully expressive of Sangiovese. The length, persistence, and aftertaste are of notable importance and echo the fruit first felt on the nose.</p>',100.00,0.00,0,'[]','[]','[]',NULL,0,0,0,12,'IT-ABPC',1,NULL,'amount',NULL,'amount','0',0.00,0.00,0,'ANTINORI BADIA A PASSIGNANO GRAN SELEZIONE CHIANTI CLASSICO RISERVA DOCG','Country: Italy\r\n\r\nAn intense ruby red in color, the wine shows aromas of ripe fruit, at times of maximum ripeness, but with a total respect for the grape variety and an excellently maintained freshness. The notes of the fruit and of the oak fuse in harmonious balance with minty balsamic notes and suggestions of graphite. The rich palate, with supple and balanced tannins, is vibrant and fully expressive of Sangiovese. The length, persistence, and aftertaste are of notable importance and echo the fruit first felt on the nose.','uploads/products/photos/IT-ABPC-.1.jpg',NULL,'antinori-badia-a-passignano-gran-selezione-chianti-classico-riserva-docg-it-abpc',0,0.00,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,'2021-03-23 09:04:43','2021-04-09 05:24:30',0),(1649,'ANTINORI MARCHESE ANTINORI CHIANTI CLASSICO RISERVA DOCG','seller',1544,12,79,96,201,'[\"uploads\\/products\\/photos\\/IT-ATTCC-.1.jpg\"]','uploads/products/photos/IT-ATTCC-.1.jpg','youtube',NULL,'','<p>Country: Italy, Chianti</p><p></p><p>Tasting Notes: An intense ruby red in color, the wine offers a fruity and floral nose with additional notes of spices and toasted oak. The palate is supple and balanced and the toasty and fruity sensations linger on a fragrant and persistent finish.</p><p></p><p>Varietal: Blend of Sangiovese & Cabernet Sauvignon</p>',89.00,0.00,0,'[]','[]','[]',NULL,0,0,0,12,'IT-ATTCC',1,NULL,'amount',NULL,'amount','0',0.00,0.00,0,'ANTINORI MARCHESE ANTINORI CHIANTI CLASSICO RISERVA DOCG','Country: Italy, Chianti\r\n\r\nTasting Notes: An intense ruby red in color, the wine offers a fruity and floral nose with additional notes of spices and toasted oak. The palate is supple and balanced and the toasty and fruity sensations linger on a fragrant and persistent finish.\r\n\r\nVarietal: Blend of Sangiovese & Cabernet Sauvignon','uploads/products/photos/IT-ATTCC-.1.jpg',NULL,'antinori-marchese-antinori-chianti-classico-riserva-docg-it-attcc',0,0.00,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,'2021-03-23 09:04:43','2021-04-09 05:24:51',0),(1650,'ANTINORI PIAN DELLE VIGNE ROSSO DI MONTALCINO','seller',1544,12,79,96,201,'[\"uploads\\/products\\/photos\\/IT- APDVRM-.1.jpg\"]','uploads/products/photos/IT- APDVRM-.1.jpg','youtube',NULL,'','<p>Country: Italy, Tuscany</p><p></p><p>Tasting Notes: An intense and luminous ruby red in color, the wine shows a complex nose of cherries, plums, and red berry fruit. The palate is vigorous and vibrant, and a lovely acidic vein fused with much flavor make this and ample and balanced wine. The finish and aftertaste are persistent and lingering.</p>',60.00,0.00,0,'[]','[]','[]',NULL,0,0,0,12,'IT- APDVRM',1,NULL,'amount',NULL,'amount','0',0.00,0.00,0,'ANTINORI PIAN DELLE VIGNE ROSSO DI MONTALCINO','Country: Italy, Tuscany\r\n\r\nTasting Notes: An intense and luminous ruby red in color, the wine shows a complex nose of cherries, plums, and red berry fruit. The palate is vigorous and vibrant, and a lovely acidic vein fused with much flavor make this and ample and balanced wine. The finish and aftertaste are persistent and lingering.','uploads/products/photos/IT- APDVRM-.1.jpg',NULL,'antinori-pian-delle-vigne-rosso-di-montalcino-it--apdvrm',0,0.00,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,'2021-03-23 09:04:43','2021-04-09 05:25:20',0),(1651,'ANTINORI PIAN DELLE VIGNE BRUNELLO DI MONTALCINO DOCG','seller',1544,12,79,96,201,'[\"uploads\\/products\\/photos\\/IT-APDVBM-.1.jpg\"]','uploads/products/photos/IT-APDVBM-.1.jpg','youtube',NULL,'','<p>Country: Italy</p><p></p><p>Pian delle Vigne is characterized by complex and intense aromas: floral notes accompanied by fragrant sensations of wild cherries, raspberries, and perceptible presence of plums, mints, and eucalyptus. Balanced and ample on the palate with full and intense flavours and texture, this Sangiovese is elegant and noble in the tactile sensations of its tannins and very mineral as well, a Brunello which promises significant expressive possibilities as it ages and develops over time.</p>',116.00,0.00,0,'[]','[]','[]',NULL,0,0,0,12,'IT-APDVBM',1,NULL,'amount',NULL,'amount','0',0.00,0.00,0,'ANTINORI PIAN DELLE VIGNE BRUNELLO DI MONTALCINO DOCG','Country: Italy\r\n\r\nPian delle Vigne is characterized by complex and intense aromas: floral notes accompanied by fragrant sensations of wild cherries, raspberries, and perceptible presence of plums, mints, and eucalyptus. Balanced and ample on the palate with full and intense flavours and texture, this Sangiovese is elegant and noble in the tactile sensations of its tannins and very mineral as well, a Brunello which promises significant expressive possibilities as it ages and develops over time.','uploads/products/photos/IT-APDVBM-.1.jpg',NULL,'antinori-pian-delle-vigne-brunello-di-montalcino-docg-it-apdvbm',0,0.00,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,'2021-03-23 09:04:43','2021-04-09 05:25:42',0),(1652,'CERVARO DELLA SALA UMBRIA IGT','seller',1544,1,1,2,0,'[\"uploads\\/products\\/photos\\/IT-ACDSC-.1.jpg\"]','uploads/products/photos/IT-ACDSC-.1.jpg',NULL,NULL,NULL,'<p>Country: Italy</p><p></p><p>Rich, complex, and fresh bouquet of hazelnut butter, vanilla, and white flowers. It is elegant on the palate and extremely savory, crisp, and vibrant. The delicate toasty sensations of the oak barrels blend harmoniously with the structure of the wine, fully bringing out the notes of both tropical and citrus fruit.</p>',99.00,0.00,0,'[]','[]','[]',NULL,0,1,0,12,'IT-ACDSC',1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'0',0.00,0.00,0,'CERVARO DELLA SALA UMBRIA IGT','Country: Italy\n\nRich, complex, and fresh bouquet of hazelnut butter, vanilla, and white flowers. It is elegant on the palate and extremely savory, crisp, and vibrant. The delicate toasty sensations of the oak barrels blend harmoniously with the structure of the wine, fully bringing out the notes of both tropical and citrus fruit.','uploads/products/photos/IT-ACDSC-.1.jpg',NULL,'cervaro-della-sala-umbria-igt-it-acdsc',0,0.00,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,'2021-03-23 09:04:43','2021-04-08 05:13:25',0),(1653,'CUSUMANO NERO D\'AVOLA TERRE SICILIANE IGT','seller',1544,12,79,96,212,'[\"uploads\\/products\\/photos\\/IT-CNDA-.1.jpg\"]','uploads/products/photos/IT-CNDA-.1.jpg','youtube',NULL,'','<p>Country: Italy</p><p></p><p>deep ruby colour; dark fruit with coffee and spice aromas; dry, medium body; cherry and plum flavours with balanced acidity; ripe tannins in soft medium length finish</p>',53.00,0.00,0,'[]','[]','[]',NULL,0,1,0,12,'IT-CNDA',1,NULL,'amount',NULL,'amount','0',0.00,0.00,0,'CUSUMANO NERO D\'AVOLA TERRE SICILIANE IGT','Country: Italy\r\n\r\ndeep ruby colour; dark fruit with coffee and spice aromas; dry, medium body; cherry and plum flavours with balanced acidity; ripe tannins in soft medium length finish','uploads/products/photos/IT-CNDA-.1.jpg',NULL,'cusumano-nero-d-avola-terre-siciliane-igt-it-cnda',0,0.00,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,'2021-03-23 09:04:43','2021-04-09 05:26:48',0),(1654,'SAN MARZANO IL PUMO CHARDONNAY 2019','seller',1544,12,79,97,222,'[\"uploads\\/products\\/photos\\/IT-SMIPC-.1.jpg\"]','uploads/products/photos/IT-SMIPC-.1.jpg','youtube',NULL,'','<p>Country: Italy</p><p></p><p>Grape  Varietal: Chardonnay </p><p></p><p>Awards: 94pts by Luca Maroni </p><p></p><p>Tasting notes: </p><p>This white is convincingly easy drinking - a whole bowl full of stone-fruit fruit generosity with a playfully round palate. Come here for that peachy flavour.</p>',38.00,0.00,0,'[]','[]','[]',NULL,0,0,0,120,'IT-SMIPC',1,NULL,'amount',NULL,'amount','0',0.00,0.00,0,'SAN MARZANO IL PUMO CHARDONNAY 2019','Country: Italy\r\n\r\nGrape  Varietal: Chardonnay \r\n\r\nAwards: 94pts by Luca Maroni \r\n\r\nTasting notes: \r\nThis white is convincingly easy drinking - a whole bowl full of stone-fruit fruit generosity with a playfully round palate. Come here for that peachy flavour.','uploads/products/photos/IT-SMIPC-.1.jpg',NULL,'san-marzano-il-pumo-chardonnay-2019-it-smipc',0,0.00,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,'2021-03-23 09:04:43','2021-04-09 05:27:17',0),(1655,'SAN MARZANO EDDA BIANCO 2019','seller',1544,12,79,97,222,'[\"uploads\\/products\\/photos\\/IT-SMEB-.1.jpg\"]','uploads/products/photos/IT-SMEB-.1.jpg','youtube',NULL,'','<p>Country: Italy</p><p></p><p>Grape Varietals: Chardonnay 80%, Moscatello Selvatico 15%, Fiano 5%</p><p></p><p>Awards: LM 99points</p><p></p><p>Tasting notes:</p><p></p><p>\'Wines like this seemed like mirages up to ten years ago. Simple, marvellous fruit: now Mediterranean, now tropical, now temperate, now rich in essences, while the same grapes seem especially sappy and fully ripe. No defects or oxidised hints that alter its limpidity and expressive integrity. With the sweetness of the fruit that releases oak\'s mint, with the candour of icing and jasmine. With a touch of pulpy viscous density, a palatial balance of absolute roundness and yet of an innervating gustatory acidity. A wine of maximum analytical and sensorial value that, like the rainbow, in a crystalline way, spreads its wonderful wheel of aromas.\" - 99 POINTS, LUCA MARONI</p>',55.00,0.00,0,'[]','[]','[]',NULL,0,0,0,60,'IT-SMEB',1,NULL,'amount',NULL,'amount','0',0.00,0.00,0,'SAN MARZANO EDDA BIANCO 2019','Country: Italy\r\n\r\nGrape Varietals: Chardonnay 80%, Moscatello Selvatico 15%, Fiano 5%\r\n\r\nAwards: LM 99points\r\n\r\nTasting notes:\r\n\r\n\'Wines like this seemed like mirages up to ten years ago. Simple, marvellous fruit: now Mediterranean, now tropical, now temperate, now rich in essences, while the same grapes seem especially sappy and fully ripe. No defects or oxidised hints that alter its limpidity and expressive integrity. With the sweetness of the fruit that releases oak\'s mint, with the candour of icing and jasmine. With a touch of pulpy viscous density, a palatial balance of absolute roundness and yet of an innervating gustatory acidity. A wine of maximum analytical and sensorial value that, like the rainbow, in a crystalline way, spreads its wonderful wheel of aromas.\" - 99 POINTS, LUCA MARONI','uploads/products/photos/IT-SMEB-.1.jpg',NULL,'san-marzano-edda-bianco-2019-it-smeb',0,0.00,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,'2021-03-23 09:04:44','2021-04-09 05:27:37',0),(1656,'SAN MARZANO F NEGROAMARO 2018','seller',1544,12,79,96,222,'[\"uploads\\/products\\/photos\\/IT-SMFN-.1.jpg\"]','uploads/products/photos/IT-SMFN-.1.jpg','youtube',NULL,'','<p>Country: Italy</p><p></p><p>Grape Varietal: Negroamaro </p><p></p><p>Awards:</p><p></p><p>BERLINER WEIN TROPHY 2020 – WINTER TASTING – GOLD MEDAL</p><p>MUNDUS VINI 2020 – SPRING TASTING – SILVER MEDAL</p><p>ANNUARIO DEI MIGLIORI VINI ITALIANI LUCA MARONI 2020 – 1ST BEST RED WINE (98 POINTS)</p><p>NEW ZEALAND INTERNATIONAL WINE SHOW 2019 – GOLD MEDAL</p><p></p><p>Tasting Notes: </p><p></p><p>“We searched long and hard among the oldest Negramaro vineyards of Salento for the perfect grapes to express the soul of this noble vine. We selected only three vineyards and “F” is the name we chose to give them. “F” as in Feudi di San Marzano. A part of our history, this letter has become a mark of quality for Negramaro, a symbol of our passion for this ancient and challenging grape.” 1st Best Red Wine of Italy (98 Points) by Luca Maroni, wine critic</p>',83.00,0.00,0,'[]','[]','[]',NULL,0,0,0,90,'IT-SMFN',1,NULL,'amount',NULL,'amount','0',0.00,0.00,0,'SAN MARZANO F NEGROAMARO 2018','Country: Italy\r\n\r\nGrape Varietal: Negroamaro \r\n\r\nAwards:\r\n\r\nBERLINER WEIN TROPHY 2020 – WINTER TASTING – GOLD MEDAL\r\nMUNDUS VINI 2020 – SPRING TASTING – SILVER MEDAL\r\nANNUARIO DEI MIGLIORI VINI ITALIANI LUCA MARONI 2020 – 1ST BEST RED WINE (98 POINTS)\r\nNEW ZEALAND INTERNATIONAL WINE SHOW 2019 – GOLD MEDAL\r\n\r\nTasting Notes: \r\n\r\n“We searched long and hard among the oldest Negramaro vineyards of Salento for the perfect grapes to express the soul of this noble vine. We selected only three vineyards and “F” is the name we chose to give them. “F” as in Feudi di San Marzano. A part of our history, this letter has become a mark of quality for Negramaro, a symbol of our passion for this ancient and challenging grape.” 1st Best Red Wine of Italy (98 Points) by Luca Maroni, wine critic','uploads/products/photos/IT-SMFN-.1.jpg',NULL,'san-marzano-f-negroamaro-2018-it-smfn',0,0.00,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,'2021-03-23 09:04:44','2021-04-09 05:28:09',0),(1657,'SAN MARZANO COLLEZIONE CINQUANTA +4','seller',1544,12,79,96,222,'[\"uploads\\/products\\/photos\\/IT-SMCC-.1.jpg\"]','uploads/products/photos/IT-SMCC-.1.jpg','youtube',NULL,'','<p>Grape Varietal: Primitivo and Negroamaro</p><p></p><p>Wine awards: </p><p></p><p>Concours Mondial de Bruxelles 2019: Gold Medal </p><p>Decanter World Wine Awards 2019: Gold Medal </p><p>Monde Selection Bruxelles 2019: Gold Medal</p><p>G 100 International Wine & Spirits Awards 2019: Gold Medal</p><p>Luca Maroni Annual Italian Wine Awards 2019: 98 Points & Best Red</p><p></p><p>Tasting Notes: </p><p></p><p>\"This features aromas of rich chocolate, vanilla and leather, with plenty of jammy notes too. Gentle tannins, well balanced freshness and acidity. Smoky finish. Delicious.\'\'</p><p></p><p>Wine awards: </p><p></p><p>Concours Mondial de Bruxelles 2019: Gold Medal </p><p>Decanter World Wine Awards 2019: Gold Medal </p><p>Monde Selection Bruxelles 2019: Gold Medal</p><p>G 100 International Wine & Spirits Awards 2019: Gold Medal</p><p>Luca Maroni Annual Italian Wine Awards 2019: 98 Points & Best Red</p><p></p><p>Tasting Notes: </p><p></p><p>\"This features aromas of rich chocolate, vanilla and leather, with plenty of jammy notes too. Gentle tannins, well balanced freshness and acidity. Smoky finish. Delicious.\'\'</p>',65.00,0.00,0,'[]','[]','[]',NULL,0,0,0,120,'IT-SMCC',1,NULL,'amount',NULL,'amount','0',0.00,0.00,0,'SAN MARZANO COLLEZIONE CINQUANTA +4','Grape Varietal: Primitivo and Negroamaro\r\n\r\nWine awards: \r\n\r\nConcours Mondial de Bruxelles 2019: Gold Medal \r\nDecanter World Wine Awards 2019: Gold Medal \r\nMonde Selection Bruxelles 2019: Gold Medal\r\nG 100 International Wine & Spirits Awards 2019: Gold Medal\r\nLuca Maroni Annual Italian Wine Awards 2019: 98 Points & Best Red\r\n\r\nTasting Notes: \r\n\r\n\"This features aromas of rich chocolate, vanilla and leather, with plenty of jammy notes too. Gentle tannins, well balanced freshness and acidity. Smoky finish. Delicious.\'\'\r\n\r\nWine awards: \r\n\r\nConcours Mondial de Bruxelles 2019: Gold Medal \r\nDecanter World Wine Awards 2019: Gold Medal \r\nMonde Selection Bruxelles 2019: Gold Medal\r\nG 100 International Wine & Spirits Awards 2019: Gold Medal\r\nLuca Maroni Annual Italian Wine Awards 2019: 98 Points & Best Red\r\n\r\nTasting Notes: \r\n\r\n\"This features aromas of rich chocolate, vanilla and leather, with plenty of jammy notes too. Gentle tannins, well balanced freshness and acidity. Smoky finish. Delicious.\'\'','uploads/products/photos/IT-SMCC-.1.jpg',NULL,'san-marzano-collezione-cinquanta-4-it-smcc',0,0.00,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,'2021-03-23 09:04:44','2021-04-09 05:28:31',0),(1658,'FONTODI FLACCIANELLO DELLA PIEVE COLLI DELLA TOSCANA 2016','seller',1544,12,79,96,213,'[\"uploads\\/products\\/photos\\/IT-FFPT-.1.jpg\"]','uploads/products/photos/IT-FFPT-.1.jpg','youtube',NULL,'','<p>Country: Italy</p><p></p><p>Grape: 100% Sangiovese </p><p></p><p>Awards: 100pts (RP)</p><p></p><p>Tasting Note: </p><p></p><p>Outer quote mark Fontodi\'s 2016 Flaccianello della Pieve is a masterpiece. This review represents a composite of notes from two separate tasting sessions, one at the winery and a second bottle tasted repeatedly over the course of 24 hours at my own pace. In the case of the second sample, it ended up in a blind flight next to the 2016 Masseto, and as beautiful as that Merlot-based wine is, this wine paints an even more beautiful portrait of a perfect Tuscan landscape, thanks to that tangy Sangiovese typicity. This vintage shows amazing depth and poise, with a sheer sense of elegance that comes from the undisputed quality of fruit achieved in this balanced vintage. The bouquet opens to dark cherry, blue flower and tilled earth. The tannins are taut, almost crunchy, and the wine offers profound pedigree and persistence that is driven by the evident acidity. That depth is what stands out most. Until the 2013 vintage, Flaccianello was aged in barrique for 24 months. After that vintage, six months of the total aging time is spent in botte instead. This 2016 vintage includes a small part from clay amphorae for the first time. This slight change in the relationship of wine to barrel size has resulted in a more elegant and finessed wine. That point is especially underlined in this vintage. Because of cool spring temperatures during the flowering, yields were reduced by 20% in 2016 compared to 2015.</p><p></p>',298.00,0.00,0,'[]','[]','[]',NULL,0,1,0,3,'IT-FFPT',1,NULL,'amount',NULL,'amount','0',0.00,0.00,0,'FONTODI FLACCIANELLO DELLA PIEVE COLLI DELLA TOSCANA 2016','Country: Italy\r\n\r\nGrape: 100% Sangiovese \r\n\r\nAwards: 100pts (RP)\r\n\r\nTasting Note: \r\n\r\nOuter quote mark Fontodi\'s 2016 Flaccianello della Pieve is a masterpiece. This review represents a composite of notes from two separate tasting sessions, one at the winery and a second bottle tasted repeatedly over the course of 24 hours at my own pace. In the case of the second sample, it ended up in a blind flight next to the 2016 Masseto, and as beautiful as that Merlot-based wine is, this wine paints an even more beautiful portrait of a perfect Tuscan landscape, thanks to that tangy Sangiovese typicity. This vintage shows amazing depth and poise, with a sheer sense of elegance that comes from the undisputed quality of fruit achieved in this balanced vintage. The bouquet opens to dark cherry, blue flower and tilled earth. The tannins are taut, almost crunchy, and the wine offers profound pedigree and persistence that is driven by the evident acidity. That depth is what stands out most. Until the 2013 vintage, Flaccianello was aged in barrique for 24 months. After that vintage, six months of the total aging time is spent in botte instead. This 2016 vintage includes a small part from clay amphorae for the first time. This slight change in the relationship of wine to barrel size has resulted in a more elegant and finessed wine. That point is especially underlined in this vintage. Because of cool spring temperatures during the flowering, yields were reduced by 20% in 2016 compared to 2015.','uploads/products/photos/IT-FFPT-.1.jpg',NULL,'fontodi-flaccianello-della-pieve-colli-della-toscana-2016-it-ffpt',0,0.00,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,'2021-03-23 09:04:44','2021-04-09 05:29:11',0),(1659,'MASSETO 2014','seller',1544,12,79,96,218,'[\"uploads\\/products\\/photos\\/IT-M14-.1.jpg\"]','uploads/products/photos/IT-M14-.1.jpg','youtube',NULL,'','<p>Country: Italy</p><p></p><p>The Masseto is a great and prestigious expression of Merlot of the zone of Bolgheri ,a king of the Italian wine. The notes of small red fruits are perfectly integrated with spicy notes. The taste is harmonic and balanced, a perfect dosage of elegant and structure, freshness and smoothness, with an infinity final. Aromas of cedar, red berry, pipe tobacco and a whiff of toasted oak lift out of the glass. The elegant but restrained palate delivers red cherry, cassis, licorice and exotic spice alongside bright acidity and fine-grained polished tannins. It\'s an admirable effort for the cool wet vintage</p>',1028.00,0.00,0,'[]','[]','[]',NULL,0,1,1,5,'IT-M14',1,NULL,'amount',NULL,'amount','0',0.00,0.00,0,'MASSETO 2014','Country: Italy\r\n\r\nThe Masseto is a great and prestigious expression of Merlot of the zone of Bolgheri ,a king of the Italian wine. The notes of small red fruits are perfectly integrated with spicy notes. The taste is harmonic and balanced, a perfect dosage of elegant and structure, freshness and smoothness, with an infinity final. Aromas of cedar, red berry, pipe tobacco and a whiff of toasted oak lift out of the glass. The elegant but restrained palate delivers red cherry, cassis, licorice and exotic spice alongside bright acidity and fine-grained polished tannins. It\'s an admirable effort for the cool wet vintage','uploads/products/photos/IT-M14-.1.jpg',NULL,'masseto-2014-it-m14',0,0.00,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,'2021-03-23 09:04:44','2021-04-12 07:15:28',0),(1660,'CHAMPAGNE M.HASLINGER & FILS NV','seller',1544,12,79,99,217,'[\"uploads\\/products\\/photos\\/FR- CMHF-.1.jpg\"]','uploads/products/photos/FR- CMHF-.1.jpg','youtube',NULL,'','<p>Country: France</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Founded in 1869, the long-established Maison G.H. Martell procures grapes from its own 200 hectares and 550 growers, producing 10 million bottles a year, the sixth largest. Unlike other major Maisons, Moet Chandon, etc., it is a family business on this scale, and it has continued to be a work-popular quality, with champagne and brandy making from generation to generation without looking to other industries.</p>\n<p>In addition, the sense of security for its history and quality, such as its high reputation from Gidd Achette, the country\'s most prestigious wine guide magazine, and its track record of being adopted by airlines around the world, is by far the best in Champagne.</p>\n<p>The new champagne brand that Martell is developing is Haslinger Aslange.</p>\n<p>It features a simple, lean and elegant design and a delicate taste to match&nbsp; Japanese cuisine with traditional assemblage using Pinot Noir, Pinot Meunier and Chardonnay.</p>',80.00,0.00,0,'[]','[]','[]',NULL,0,1,1,24,'FR- CMHF',1,NULL,'amount',NULL,'amount','0',0.00,0.00,0,'CHAMPAGNE M.HASLINGER & FILS NV','Country: France\r\n\r\nFounded in 1869, the long-established Maison G.H. Martell procures\r\ngrapes from its own 200 hectares and 550 growers, producing 10 million\r\nbottles a year, the sixth largest.\r\nUnlike other major Maisons, Moet Chandon, etc., it is a family business\r\non this scale, and it has continued to be a work-popular quality, with\r\nchampagne and brandy making from generation to generation without\r\nlooking to other industries.\r\nIn addition, the sense of security for its history and quality, such as its\r\nhigh reputation from Gidd Achette, the country\'s most prestigious wine\r\nguide magazine, and its track record of being adopted by airlines around\r\nthe world, is by far the best in Champagne.\r\nThe new champagne brand that Martell is developing is Haslinger\r\nAslange.\r\nIt features a simple, lean and elegant design and a delicate taste to\r\nmatch Japanese cuisine with traditional assemblage using Pinot Noir,\r\nPinot Meunier and Chardonnay.','uploads/products/photos/FR- CMHF-.1.jpg',NULL,'champagne-m-haslinger-fils-nv-fr--cmhf',0,0.00,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,'2021-03-23 09:04:44','2021-04-12 07:15:25',0),(1661,'CHATEAU RAMAGE LA BATTISE AOC HAUT-MEDOC 2011/2015','seller',1544,12,79,96,208,'[\"uploads\\/products\\/photos\\/FR- CRLB-.1.jpg\"]